    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1359">

                <pb facs="1615" n="1417" xml:id="pg1417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/7–2645: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1359<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in the Conversations
                        Concerning Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1359-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-26T13:00:00+02:00">July 26, 1945—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4505. From Childs.</p>
                <p>Meyrier informed us today that British and French were concerting together on the
                    form of invitation to the USSR to participate in the Tangier conversations to
                    open in Paris on August 6 and that it was hoped to arrive at a definite text
                    which would (sent Dept as 4505; repeated Tangier as 24; Madrid as 281 and London
                    as 541) be communicated to the French and British Embassies in Moscow
                    tomorrow.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1359-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1359-f1-content">
                <p>Sent over the signature of Caffery.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
